      "writtenOn": "2022-09-22T07:56:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I saw the BluetoothMapAccountItem.hashCode() implementation, and it relies on the String member variables\u0027 hashCode(). \u0027String\u0027 is a special case where the hashCode is reliable, so this test won\u0027t fail. However, even with the fact I don\u0027t recommend relying on the value of hashCode() in general.\n\nIt is because other classes\u0027 hashCode() can vary according to JVM, or to each test run with the same JVM.\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/a/785150\n\nInstead, I would suggest testing whether two equal objects\u0027 hashCode() is same.",
